# Bank transfer order, step by step, for the HTTP client of IntelliJ IDEA.
#
# Start the engine on port 8080 and zenbpm-ui as examples/README.md says, then either twin of this
# example (README "Run it"); both answer on port 8103. The model reminds after ten seconds and
# cancels after twenty-five, with the engine looking for due timers every second
# (POLL_TIMER_DELAY_SECONDS=1). Run the requests of a scenario one after the other, waiting where a
# step says so. A step which reads the order checks where it stands: a red check means "not yet",
# run it again. Every run places orders of new numbers. zenbpm-ui shows each order as an instance
# of bank-transfer-order__bank_transfer_order whose business key is the order's number.

@app = http://localhost:8103
@engine = http://localhost:8080

### BankTransferOrderIT#anOrderPaidInTimeIsShippedWithoutAReminder: 1. place an order paid by bank transfer
POST {{app}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}", "customerEmail": "jane.doe@example.com", "item": "hiking boots", "total": 89.90}

> {%
    client.global.set("inTime", response.body.orderId);
%}

### 2. the payment instructions are mailed (zenbpm-ui: the token waits at "Wait for the bank transfer")
GET {{app}}/orders/{{inTime}}

> {%
    client.test("the instructions are sent", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "AWAITING_PAYMENT", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.paymentInstructionsSent === true, "the instructions are not sent yet");
    });
%}

### 3. the bank reports the transfer, within ten seconds of the order
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "{{inTime}}", "amount": 89.90}

> {%
    client.test("the transfer pays the order", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 4. shipped, and nobody was reminded
GET {{app}}/orders/{{inTime}}

> {%
    client.test("shipped without a reminder", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "SHIPPED", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.trackingNumber.startsWith("PARCEL-"), "no parcel");
        client.assert(response.body.reminderSent === false, "the customer was reminded");
    });
%}

### 5. the workflow is completed: the message ended the wait, and its reminder with it
GET {{engine}}/v1/process-instances?businessKey={{inTime}}

> {%
    client.test("the workflow is completed", function () {
        const instances = response.body.partitions.flatMap(function (partition) {
            return partition.items;
        });
        client.assert(instances.length === 1 && instances[0].state === "completed", "not completed yet");
    });
%}

### BankTransferOrderIT#aCustomerWhoPaysLateIsRemindedAndTheOrderShippedAllTheSame: 1. place an order
POST {{app}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}", "customerEmail": "jane.doe@example.com", "item": "rain jacket", "total": 149.00}

> {%
    client.global.set("late", response.body.orderId);
%}

### 2. wait more than ten seconds: the customer is reminded (the application logs the mail), and the order keeps waiting
GET {{app}}/orders/{{late}}

> {%
    client.test("reminded, still waiting", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "AWAITING_PAYMENT", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.reminderSent === true, "not reminded yet");
    });
%}

### 3. the bank reports the transfer, before the deadline at twenty-five seconds
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "{{late}}", "amount": 149.00}

### 4. shipped all the same
GET {{app}}/orders/{{late}}

> {%
    client.test("shipped", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "SHIPPED", "status is " + response.body.status);
    });
%}

### BankTransferOrderIT#anOrderNotPaidByTheDeadlineIsCancelledAndALateTransferRefused: 1. place an order nobody pays
POST {{app}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}", "customerEmail": "jane.doe@example.com", "item": "tent", "total": 249.00}

> {%
    client.global.set("unpaid", response.body.orderId);
%}

### 2. wait more than twenty-five seconds: the deadline cancelled the order and released its stock
GET {{app}}/orders/{{unpaid}}

> {%
    client.test("cancelled", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "CANCELLED", "status is " + response.body.status);
        client.assert(response.body.stockReleased === true, "the stock is not released");
    });
%}

### 3. a transfer after the deadline is refused: accounting pays it back
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "{{unpaid}}", "amount": 249.00}

> {%
    client.test("409 Conflict", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 409, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### BankTransferOrderIT#aTransferWhichMatchesNoWaitingOrderIsLeftToAccounting: 1. place an order
POST {{app}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}", "customerEmail": "jane.doe@example.com", "item": "sleeping bag", "total": 89.90}

> {%
    client.global.set("mismatched", response.body.orderId);
%}

### 2. a transfer of the wrong amount
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "{{mismatched}}", "amount": 8.99}

> {%
    client.test("422 Unprocessable Content", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 422, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 3. a transfer whose reference no order has
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"reference": "ORD-UNKNOWN", "amount": 89.90}

> {%
    client.test("422 Unprocessable Content", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 422, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### 4. the order keeps waiting for its money
GET {{app}}/orders/{{mismatched}}

> {%
    client.test("still waiting", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.status === "AWAITING_PAYMENT", "status is " + response.body.status);
    });
%}

### BankTransferOrderIT#anInvalidOrderIsRefused: a total with three decimals
POST {{app}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}", "customerEmail": "jane.doe@example.com", "item": "hiking boots", "total": 89.905}

> {%
    client.test("400 Bad Request", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

### BankTransferOrderIT#anIncompleteTransferIsRefused: a transfer without a reference
POST {{app}}/bank/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": 89.90}

> {%
    client.test("400 Bad Request", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 400, "answered " + response.status);
    });
%}

# Not here, because a client which sends one request after the other cannot cause them:
# BankTransferOrderIT#aTransferWhichArrivesWithTheDeadlineIsPaidBack and
# BankTransferOrderIT#aCustomerWhoHasJustPaidIsNotReminded need a transfer in the second between a
# timer firing and its task; BankTransferOrderIT#aShipmentRepeatedAfterAFailureSendsOneParcel needs
# a failed task; BankTransferOrderIT#anOrderPlacedTwiceAtOnceIsTakenOnce and
# BankTransferOrderIT#aTransferReportedTwiceAtOnceIsAcceptedOnce send requests at the same moment.
